 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A sealed-body metal alloy resistor of metallized material. The part is sulfur resistant, halogen-free and lead-free, with an ultra-low temperature coefficient, high rated power and ultra-long-term stability."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power and temperature",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Full rated power applies up to 70 °C ambient. Above that the allowed power falls in a straight line to zero at 170 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board layout",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The recommended land pattern joins trace copper to the outer side of each pad and runs a narrow trace, the inductive path, from the inner corner of each pad."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Protect the body surface from knocks and scratches and keep sharp tools off it: scratches can shift the resistance or cause failure. Keep mechanical stress off the part when fitting and in use. Long-term operation above the rated power makes the resistance drift; at high temperature or with poor heat dissipation the power is derated along the derating curve. Parts stay in the tape until use, since oxidation spoils solderability."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Store at 5 to 35 °C below 65 % RH, humidity as low as possible, in a clean dry place free of harmful gases, in the original packing. Shelf life under these conditions is one year; stock older than a year has its surface inspected for oxidation and is tested for solderability before use."
  }
 ],
